IO-61: use the continuity tables' gallons factor in the summary tables

DefaultReportPlugin copied legacy statsrpt.c's summary-table factor,
7.48 gal/ft3 (28.317 L/ft3), next to the continuity tables' factor
0.64632 / 86400 (2.4466 / 86400), so the same water printed 0.0074 %
smaller in the summary tables. Use the continuity factor for both.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-61_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/plugins/DefaultReportPlugin.cpp b/src/engine/plugins/DefaultReportPlugin.cpp
index 36a8dbb..0c601fa 100644
--- a/src/engine/plugins/DefaultReportPlugin.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/plugins/DefaultReportPlugin.cpp
@@ -896,9 +896,9 @@ void DefaultReportPlugin::write_results(std::FILE* f,
     const double len_ucf   = du.length;      // ft  → ft | m  (depth/HGL/velocity)
     const double svol_ucf  = du.volume;      // ft³ → ft³ | m³ (storage volume)
     const char*  len_word  = du.length_word; // Feet | Meters
-    // legacy statsrpt.c's own factor for every summary-table volume
-    // (7.48 gal/ft3, 28.317 L/ft3 — not the massbal/continuity constants).
-    const double Vcf       = si_report ? 28.317 / 1.0e6 : 7.48 / 1.0e6;
+    // factor for every summary-table volume: the same as the continuity
+    // tables' 10^6 gal (ltr) column below, MGDperCFS (MLDperCFS) / SECperDAY.
+    const double Vcf       = si_report ? 2.4466 / 86400.0 : 0.64632 / 86400.0;
     const char*  vol_word  = du.mvol_word;    // 10^6 gal | 10^6 ltr
     // legacy report.c continuity factors: UCF(LENGTH) * UCF(LANDAREA) for
     // acre-feet / hectare-m, and MGDperCFS (MLDperCFS) / SECperDAY for the
